WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:06.680
Yesterday, rising Republican star Daniel Cameron,
who's the attorney general of Kentucky, announced

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:14.429
charges against officers involved in the fatal
shooting by police of black woman Briona Taylor

00:00:14.429 --> 00:00:16.290
and very few charges were outlined.

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:20.590
And now protests and unrest are once again
rising.

00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:22.930
And we're going to talk about all of it as
a reminder.

00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:29.720
The story here is of 26 year old Briona Taylor,
who was killed in her own home when three

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:36.079
Louisville, Kentucky, police officers executed
what's known as a no knock warrant.

00:00:36.079 --> 00:00:42.550
We've talked about no knock warrants many
times before and the the serious concerns

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:47.490
about the use of no knock warrants, particularly
related to drug crimes.

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:50.590
This was related to a drug investigation.

00:00:50.590 --> 00:00:56.580
Daniel Cameron said, listen, officers did
announce themselves as they executed the no

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:58.050
knock warrant.

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:03.650
Of course, the big picture, the red alert
is that officers used this warrant to search

00:01:03.650 --> 00:01:07.830
Briona Taylor's home for someone who did not
live there.

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:10.110
No drugs were found in the apartment.

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:14.960
And what ultimately transpired is that Briona
Taylor's boyfriend having no idea that it

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:18.440
was law enforcement in their home because
remember, there were no drugs there.

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:20.650
The person they were looking for wasn't there.

00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:24.720
Brianna Taylor's boyfriend started shooting
in what he believed was self-defense from

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:26.150
potentially an armed intruder.

00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:30.350
And Briona Taylor ended up killed in the gunfight
that ensued.

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:33.110
Now, one other note before we outline the
charges.

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:36.850
Yesterday's announcement was about criminal
charges.

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:39.890
The civil peace was settled last week.

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:44.080
The city settled the lawsuit against the three
officers involved.

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:47.610
The lawsuit was brought by Brianna Taylor's
mother.

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:52.980
And the city has agreed to pay to meet Tamika
Polmar 12 million dollars, and they've agreed

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:55.150
to enact police reforms.

00:01:55.150 --> 00:02:01.110
Now, in terms of the criminal charges, one
of the three officers charged with wanton

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:03.410
endangerment.

00:02:03.410 --> 00:02:04.410
Wanton endangerment.

00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:09.039
And that is not actually related to the death
of Briona Taylor, the wanton endangerment

00:02:09.039 --> 00:02:15.460
is because of the discharge of the officers
firearm inside of the apartment.

00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:18.000
It put neighbors at risk.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:19.050
That's the charge.

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:23.010
Two other officers who fired shots not charged
at all.

00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:29.700
So, in essence, nobody was charged for the
actual killing of Briona Taylor.

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:36.520
This has predictably led to significant unrest
and protests have started.

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:38.120
And the protests continue to build.

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:43.200
And it's quite possible that the next 24,
48, 72, 96 hours are going to see even more

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:44.200
of it.

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:50.599
Authorities saying that two officers were
shot and wounded last night in Louisville.

00:02:50.599 --> 00:02:54.840
The interim Louisville police chief, Robert
Schroeder, said that they have a suspect in

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:58.069
custody but did not release too many additional
details.

00:02:58.069 --> 00:03:04.110
We saw demonstrations and marches in cities
including New York, Chicago, Washington, D.C.,

00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:07.530
Atlanta, Philadelphia, just massive crowds.

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:11.900
We have video of the crowd in Brooklyn near
the Barclays Center, my sort of old stomping

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:14.230
grounds when I lived in Brooklyn.

00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:20.580
That crowd eventually walked over the Manhattan
Bridge and connected with another protest

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:25.239
in Manhattan, in Chinatown and in surrounding
neighborhoods.

00:03:25.239 --> 00:03:32.349
And we are seeing these all over the country
in addition to unrest that did become more

00:03:32.349 --> 00:03:38.310
violent in Louisville, Kentucky, which is
the epicenter of this case.

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:45.080
And again, overwhelmingly peaceful protesters
with some provocateurs as as you typically

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:46.080
see.

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:47.610
So there's a few different things here.

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:50.830
Let's do the political first, maybe politically.

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:53.900
I still think this is bad for Donald Trump.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:58.480
This unrest related to racially tinged events
is not good for Donald Trump.

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:03.080
Now, Donald Trump and some of his supporters
continue to say these protests are a preview

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:04.730
of Joe Biden's America.

00:04:04.730 --> 00:04:06.940
There will be more of this if Joe Biden is
president.

00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:12.580
I believe most Americans see this and they
see it as part of the failures of the Trump

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:13.920
administration.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:18.549
Part of the failure of the ideology that Donald
Trump espouses on police use of force.

00:04:18.549 --> 00:04:20.299
And we're seeing it reflected in the polls.

00:04:20.299 --> 00:04:24.650
We don't really have to wonder after corona
virus in the economy.

00:04:24.650 --> 00:04:27.180
The third most important issue right now is
this.

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:30.069
It's race relations and this unrest and law
enforcement.

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:32.650
And Donald Trump's approval on that issue
is very, very low.

00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:36.240
So I reject the idea that this helps Donald
Trump.

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:39.939
More importantly is the issue of justice.

00:04:39.939 --> 00:04:46.240
We have a criminal legal system that is meant
to protect officers.

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:51.559
Now you can debate to what degree should officers
be protected.

00:04:51.559 --> 00:04:56.039
And I am the first to tell you that to some
degree they should be protected in the sense

00:04:56.039 --> 00:05:02.020
that being a police officer is a potentially
more dangerous job than being an accountant

00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:04.789
or being a teacher or being a cashier.

00:05:04.789 --> 00:05:09.669
And so some degree of protection makes sense
for officers.

00:05:09.669 --> 00:05:15.810
The degree to which the default is we ere
on the side of the benefit of the doubt for

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:20.559
the officers, that is allowing justice to
not be served.

00:05:20.559 --> 00:05:23.490
So, you know, I've given you the list before.

00:05:23.490 --> 00:05:26.069
We need demilitarization of police.

00:05:26.069 --> 00:05:30.960
We need special prosecutors to investigate
police, implicit bias training.

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:34.690
OK, fixing the war on drugs are Bad Actors
database.

00:05:34.690 --> 00:05:37.599
It's a very long list, ten or twelve items
which I've outlined.

00:05:37.599 --> 00:05:40.899
But the precedent that is potentially set
here is horrifying.

00:05:40.899 --> 00:05:47.560
If you have ever been associated with anyone
who is potentially a criminal, the police

00:05:47.560 --> 00:05:54.680
can in certain states issue a no knock warrant,
go into where you're you're you're living

00:05:54.680 --> 00:05:59.080
and you can end up shot dead with essentially
no repercussions.

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:03.089
Defending your home is not a defense in many
of these cases.

00:06:03.089 --> 00:06:06.659
And remember, there was a grand jury that
looked at a case.

00:06:06.659 --> 00:06:07.659
We covered it.

00:06:07.659 --> 00:06:10.550
I think I don't know if it was a year or two
years ago at this point.

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:17.469
There was a case of a woman who fired a warning
shot to get her husband to her husband, was

00:06:17.469 --> 00:06:19.789
approaching her and was abusive.

00:06:19.789 --> 00:06:23.800
She fired a warning shot in the garage and
it hit drywall.

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:27.919
She was charged more seriously than these
officers.

00:06:27.919 --> 00:06:29.999
OK, that doesn't make sense.

00:06:29.999 --> 00:06:32.990
So the system is hugely failing us.

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:38.490
We will see the degree to which unrest continues
in the next few days.

00:06:38.490 --> 00:06:42.399
But this is what we've been covering this
for a long time.

00:06:42.399 --> 00:06:44.119
There's nothing new here.

00:06:44.119 --> 00:06:49.539
But the way in which it is now playing a role
in the presidential election is certainly

00:06:49.539 --> 00:06:54.099
something the timing of which could have political
influence.

00:06:54.099 --> 00:08:09.130
And again, I do not believe it will be good
for Donald Trump.

